Reason: collision_line tested every instance of its target object, while place_meeting and the other grid queries look
only in the grid cells they cover. AM2R builds its floor and wall checks (isCollisionBottom/Top/Left/Right) and its
enemies' sight lines on collision_line against the solids: rm_a6a13 (414 instances) spent 7.3 ms a frame on it on the
Wii with Samus standing still, and 0.7 ms through the grid. An object or all target now asks the grid for the
instances under the line; when several are hit, the first in the order the whole bucket used to be walked in still
wins. An instance id target keeps the old loop.
Upstream: Speed only, every platform. Retires this patch when merged.

